{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted to gain unauthorized access to the system by executing a password spray or slow brute-force attack against multiple SSH user accounts (alice, bob, deploy, and ci-runner). The logs indicate multiple failed login attempts originating from various IPs within the 61.177.172.0/24 subnet over a sustained period, indicating automated malicious activity designed to evade standard threshold-based detection.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the offending IP address (61.177.172.13) and consider rate-limiting or blocking the broader source subnet at the firewall level.",
    "Disable password-based authentication for SSH and enforce the use of strong SSH key pairs or multi-factor authentication (MFA).",
    "Implement fail2ban or a similar intrusion prevention system to automatically ban IPs that exhibit repeated authentication failures."
  ]
}
